\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\b INITIAL INPATIENT CONSULTATION\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\ql\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\b \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\b\ul Inpatient consult to Infectious Diseases\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Consult performed by: Peter A Mead, MD\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Consult ordered by: Tiffany M. Chua, NP\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Reason for consult: Dr. Steven C Martin, MD requests our advice and opinion regarding this patient with a chronic pre-sacral collection, and, per UCC, "left sacral pain with + cultures"\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Assessment/Recommendations: Please see Assessment section below\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f3\fs24\lang1033\hich\f3\dbch\f3\loch\f3\cf2\fs24\zwnj\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22\b \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf5\fs22\b Preferred Language:  \plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Polish - telephone interpreter used\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f5\fs24\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf6\fs24\b Subjective\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf7\fs22\b History Of Present Illness\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 History is from chart and primary team's interview (for which I was present).\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Several attempts at interviewing patient myself were impractical as patient was engaged with other providers\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Waclawa Garbiel is a 72 y.o. female with a distant history of rectal cancer (initial surgery in 2007 in Poland, with ?neoadjuvant chemotherapy/XRT) - apparently had an ostomy for several months then 
reversed, more recently diagnosed with stage IIIC uterine clear cell carcinoma, found in 10/2023 on endometrial biopsy done for post-menopausal bleeding s/p robot-assisted TLH, BSO, SLND on 12/2023 [Dr. Sonoda] \plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Operative note reads in part: "filmy adhesions between colon and the posterior uterus, small bowel adherent to the presacral area suspected serosal disease at the fundus"\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Patient then received adjuvant carboplatin/paclitaxel on 1->5/2024 (Dr. Sabbatini) but by 2/2025 imaging suspected to have recurrence in inguinal and aortocaval lymph nodes.\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 We do not have records from 4-10/2025 - but 10/7/2025 note indicates:\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\li720\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f6\fs18\lang1033\hich\f6\dbch\f6\loch\f6\cf2\fs18 Northwell Health after presenting with enlarging inguinal mass and RLQ abdominal pain. Work-up was notable for "low rectal resection with a contained posterior perforation extending 
to the presacral soft tissues associated with a collection of fluid/gas measuring 6.8 x 2.3 x 7.3 cm and findings consistent with sacral osteomyelitis (?) by report. CT A/P otherwise notable for heterogeneous large right inguinal mass measuring 4.8 x 
4.6 cm and associated with enlarged right inguinal canal lymph node measuring 1.4 x 2 cm. CT chest showed no evidence of distant metastatic disease. [...] MRI total spine supported S3/S4 osteomyelitis, with no evidence of other osseous lesions. The patient 
underwent IR guided biopsy, with cultures revealing polymicrobial infection (most notably with pansensitive E coli and Enterococcus raffinosus resistant to ampicillin). She was discharged 9/27 with linezolid BID (now discontinued) and cephalexin 500 mg 
(plan  to complete 6 week course of antibiotic therapy, will follow-up with ID mid October). \plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\li0\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 S/p RA aortocaval lymph node dissection, R inguinal lymph node resection lymph node dissection, repair of R inguinal fascial defect with mesh and bone anchoring with JP placement 11/5/2025 
(Drs. Sonoda, Hespe).  Course complicated by persistent lymphatic leak\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Patient has a long-standing left pre-sacral air/fluid collection - that exists at least in the earliest CT images we have available (11/21/2023).  Next CT is from 6/7/2024 (in our system at least) and 
shows (among other things) "Persistent presacral soft tissue thickening just superior to the rectal anastomosis. The presacral air collection within the soft tissue thickening has increased, now measuring 5.3 x 1.7 cm, previously 4.3 x 1.3 cm"\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 By 7/28/2026 imaging suggested "new and increased retroperitoneal and pelvic lymphadenopathy, suspicious for nodal metastases" Started lenvatinib and pembrolizumab.\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Presented to oncology clinic on 9/1 with "increased severe left flank" pain "not relieved with oxycodone."\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 On UCC presentation she noted 1 to 1.5 weeks of constant left-sided "sciatica-like" pain.  Pain improves with walking and worsens with lying down.  She denied fever.\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 On 9/2 (HD#2) underwent IR aspiration (IR felt leading a drain may be too painful).  Post-procedure patient was started on piperacillin/tazobactam empirically (and 1 dose of piperacillin/tazobactam).\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Tmax so far is 37.8 \plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs22 \'b0C\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22  \plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Patient seen and interviewed with primary team (Solid Tumor Green).\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Patient notes considerable discomfort lying in bed, and with attempted left leg raise.\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 She notes the pain in her left groin.\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf5\fs22\b ROS\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 ROS otherwise negative in detail except as noted above. \plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f4\fs22\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf5\fs22\b Past Medical History\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 She has a past medical history of Endometrial cancer (03/14/2025), Hypertension, Osteoporosis, Peripheral neuropathy, and Rectal cancer.\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f4\fs20\lang1033\hich\f4\dbch\f4\loch\f4\cf2\fs20\par
