\ri90\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 2007 - Rectal cancer S/P resection, chemotherapy, and radiation therapy\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 US IMAGING: On 11/4/2022 showed 6 mm thick endometrium.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 METHOD OF DIAGNOSIS: Endometrial biopsy on 10/17/2023 showed high grade endometrial carcinoma with serous and clear cell features. Pathology reviewed at MSKCC showed clear cell carcinoma.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 STAGING IMAGING: CT CAP on 11/21/2023 showed\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Primary site: Left hypoenhancing uterine tumor in the endometrium/myometrium, 2.5 x 1.9 x 1.7 cm.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Regional lymph nodes: Few mildly prominent retroperitoneal nodes. For example: Left common iliac, 1.0 x 0.7 cm. Aortocaval, 0.7 x 0.6 cm.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Distant disease: Left lower lobe lung nodule, indeterminate.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 SURGERY: \plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Surgeon: Dr. Sonoda\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Date: 12/4/2023\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Unique intraoperative findings: Pelvic tissue with radiation changes, small bowel adherent into the pelvis, filmy adhesions between colon and the posterior uterus, small bowel adherent to the presacral 
area suspected serosal disease at the fundus.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Type: Robotic total hysterectomy/BSO, sentinel node mapping, and peritoneal washings.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 PATHOLOGY:\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Histology: Clear cell carcinoma\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Myometrial invasion: 14 mm out of 14 mm \plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -LVI: Low\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Cervix: Unremarkable\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Serosa: Present\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Adnexa: Unremarkable\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Sentinel lymph node: 1/3 involved lymph nodes (macrometastasis)\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -Pelvic washing: Negative\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -MSI genes: Intact \plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 -P53: Aberrant\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 1/23/24 - 05/07/24: 6 cycles of adjuvant carbo/taxol (taxol dose reduced to 135 mg/m2 due to peripheral neuropathy)\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri-15\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri90\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 2/2025 localized recurrence\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri-15\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri90\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Admission to Northwell Health in September after presenting with enlarging inguinal mass and RLQ abdominal pain. Workup was notable for "low rectal resection with a contained posterior 
perforation extending to the presacral soft tissues associated with a collection of fluid/gas measuring 6.8 x 2.3 x 7.3 cm and findings consistent with sacral osteomyelitis (?) by report. CT A/P otherwise notable for heterogeneous large right inguinal 
mass measuring 4.8 x 4.6 cm and associated with enlarged right inguinal canal lymph node measuring 1.4 x 2 cm. CT chest showed no evidence of distant metastatic disease. Tumor markers on 9/13 were as follows: Ca 12-5 11, CEA 3.9, CA 19-9 17. MRI total 
spine supported S3/S4 osteomyelitis, with no evidence of other osseous lesions. The patient underwent IR guided biopsy, with cultures revealing polymicrobial infection (most notably with pansensitive E coli and Enterococcus raffinosus resistant to ampicillin). 
She was discharged 9/27 with linezolid BID (now discontinued) and cephalexin 500 mg, with planned 6 weeks of antibiotics.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri-15\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri90\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 10/07/25: CT CAP: Increased inguinal and interaortocaval nodes consistent with metastases. Right inguinal nodes measuring 2.0 x 1.5 cm and 5.5 x 4.7 cm.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri-15\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri90\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 11/5/25: Right inguinal and para-aortic lymphadenectomy (Dr. Sonoda - Gyn Surg - and Dr. Hespe - Plastic Surg)\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 Pathology report: Overall, the findings are compatible with a metastasis from the known endometrial carcinoma.\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 1. Paracaval; Aorta-caval lymph nodes; Excision/Resection:\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22     - Metastatic carcinoma involving two of thirteen lymph nodes (2/13)\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22           - Measuring >2 mm (macrometastasis), see note\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri-15\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 \~\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\ri90\plain\f1\fs24\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22 2. Groin, Right; Right groin lymph nodes; Excision/Resection:\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22     - Metastatic carcinoma involving two of two lymph nodes (2/2), see note\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
\plain\f0\fs22\lang1033\hich\f0\dbch\f0\loch\f0\fs22           - Measuring >2 mm (macrometastasis)\plain\f5\fs22\lang1033\hich\f5\dbch\f5\loch\f5\cf2\fs22\par
